WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:13.400
Salma is three months into her first job. At the next desk, Yudha puts down the phone and sighs.

2
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:22.400
A sigh like that is a small request for attention. The psychologist John Gottman calls it a bid for connection.

3
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:31.400
She can turn toward it, miss it, or brush it off. Trust is built in these seconds, many times a day.

4
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:40.400
She turns toward it. Phone face down, chair turned, and she lets him finish. That is attention, and the other three are impossible without it.

5
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:49.400
Then she says something true about herself: I froze on my first call too. That is vulnerability. It keeps the conversation honest.

6
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:58.300
Before any advice, she says what she heard: sounds like it hit harder than you expected. That is empathy.

7
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:07.300
And she closes with an act, not a sentiment: shall we rehearse the next one at four? That is compassion.

8
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.000
Everyone agrees with the four words.

9
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.100
Few practise them in an ordinary week.

10
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.200
So pick one person and one move.

11
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:28.200
A team learns fastest when people can speak up and admit mistakes. That is psychological safety, and everyone's behaviour builds it.

12
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:35.900
From the junior seat it starts with asking: I don't follow yet, could you show me?

13
00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:42.800
Owning a mistake early: I got the file wrong, and here is the fix.

14
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.900
And thanking the person who corrected you.

15
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:53.000
Small, consistent acts from juniors change a team faster than they expect.

16
00:01:53.000 --> 00:02:02.000
On Tuesday her supervisor adds a second task to a full week. Saying no feels rude, so Salma almost says yes to both.

17
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:09.300
But a yes she cannot keep will hurt the relationship more than an honest limit.

18
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:17.000
So she states a boundary in three parts. A commitment: I want to do this well.

19
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:26.000
A limit: the report by Thursday, but not the slides too. And an option: could the slides wait until Monday?

20
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.700
Trust is built in seconds, with one person at a time.

21
00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:36.600
A boundary stated early and kindly protects the relationship.

22
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:45.600
Now it is your turn. Name one person, and choose one of the four moves to practise with them this week.
